original)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Ayurvedic (Indian)", "url": "https://sa.wikisource.org/wiki/भावप्रकाशः/पूर्वखण्डे_भावप्रकाशनिघण्टुः", "year": "16th century"}, {"agreement": "Counted: agrees with the app temperature (cool).", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cool", "corpus": "ayurvedic", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "dhānyakaṃ madhuraṃ śītaṃ kaṣāyaṃ pittanāśanam", "gloss": "Coriander is sweet, COLD, astringent, destroys bile.", "locator": "Rājanighaṇṭu 5.37", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "", "short": "Rajanighantu (c. 15th c.)", "source": "Narahari, Rājanighaṇṭu (Sanskrit original)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Ayurvedic (Indian)", "url": "http://gretil.sub.uni-goettingen.de/gretil/corpustei/transformations/plaintext/sa_narahari-rAjanighaNTu.txt", "year": "c. 15th century"}, {"agreement": "Counted: differs from the app temperature (source neutral, app cool).", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Neutral", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "子氣味辛酸平無毒", "gloss": "Seed: pungent, sour, neutral (平), not toxic.", "locator": "卷二十六 菜之一, 胡荽, 子 subsection", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "", "short": "Bencao Gangmu (1596)", "source": "李時珍, 本草綱目 (Li Shizhen, Bencao Gangmu), Siku Quanshu text", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草綱目_(四庫全書本)/", "year": "1596"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. Root and leaf, not seed.", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Warm", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "根葉氣味辛温微毒 {詵曰平微寒}", "gloss": "Root and leaf pungent, warm; Meng Shen says neutral, slightly cold.", "locator": "卷二十六, 胡荽, 根葉", "not_counted_why": "Root and leaf, not seed.", "note": "Root and leaf, not seed.", "short": "Bencao Gangmu (1596)", "source": "李時珍, 本草綱目 (Li Shizhen, Bencao Gangmu), Siku Quanshu text", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草綱目_(四庫全書本)/", "year": "1596"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. Whole herb; the entry is about the plant used as a vegetable, not the seed.", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Warm", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "胡荽 … 辛溫。微毒。", "gloss": "Coriander herb: pungent, warm.", "locator": "卷十一 菜部, 胡荽", "not_counted_why": "Whole herb; the entry is about the plant used as a vegetable, not the seed.", "note": "Whole herb; the entry is about the plant used as a vegetable, not the seed.", "short": "Bencao Congxin (1757)", "source": "吳儀洛, 本草從新 (Wu Yiluo, Bencao Congxin)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草從新", "year": "1757"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. Second-hand, and 'cooling properties' is not a thermal slot.", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cool", "corpus": "ayurvedic", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "The opinion that it has great cooling properties prevailed amongst Western physicians", "gloss": "Reports a Western opinion.", "locator": "Vol. II pp. 129-130, CORIANDRUM SATIVUM, History, Uses &c.", "not_counted_why": "Second-hand, and 'cooling properties' is not a thermal slot.", "note": "Second-hand, and 'cooling properties' is not a thermal slot.", "short": "Pharmacographia Indica II (1891)", "source": "Dymock, Warden & Hooper, Pharmacographia Indica, Vol. II", "tier": "second-hand-report", "tradition": "Ayurvedic (Indian)", "url": "https://archive.org/download/b21960343_0002/b21960343_0002_djvu.txt", "year": "1891"}], "sources_agree": false, "stored_before": {"moisture": "Neutral", "temperature": "Cool"}, "stored_value_status": {"moisture": {"status": "clear", "why": "a definite Neutral"}, "temperature": {"status": "clear", "