erature (source warm, app cool).", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Warm", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "刺蒺藜 … 辛苦而溫。", "gloss": "Spiny tribulus: pungent, bitter and warm.", "locator": "卷三 草部, 刺蒺藜", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "", "short": "Bencao Congxin (1757)", "source": "吳儀洛, 本草從新 (Wu Yiluo, Bencao Congxin)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草從新", "year": "1757"}, {"agreement": "Counted: agrees with the app temperature (cool).", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cool", "corpus": "ayurvedic", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "गोक्षुरः शीतलःस्वादुर्बलकृद्बस्तिशोधनः", "gloss": "gokṣuraḥ śītalaḥ svādur balakṛd …: gokshura is COOL, sweet, strengthening, cleanses the bladder.", "locator": "Guḍūcyādi varga 4.45", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "", "short": "Bhavaprakasha (16th c.)", "source": "Bhāvamiśra, Bhāvaprakāśa Nighaṇṭu (Sanskrit original)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Ayurvedic (Indian)", "url": "https://sa.wikisource.org/wiki/भावप्रकाशः/पूर्वखण्डे_भावप्रकाशनिघण्टुः", "year": "16th century"}, {"agreement": "Counted: agrees with the app temperature (cool).", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cool", "corpus": "ayurvedic", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "syātām ubhau gokṣurakau suśītalau balapradau tau madhurau ca bṛṃhaṇau", "gloss": "Both gokshuras are very COOL, strengthening, sweet and nourishing.", "locator": "Rājanighaṇṭu 6.43", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "", "short": "Rajanighantu (c. 15th c.)", "source": "Narahari, Rājanighaṇṭu (Sanskrit original)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Ayurvedic (Indian)", "url": "http://gretil.sub.uni-goettingen.de/gretil/corpustei/transformations/plaintext/sa_narahari-rAjanighaNTu.txt", "year": "c. 15th century"}, {"agreement": "Cou