'Of the Willow Tree', The Temperature", "not_counted_why": "Covers willows as a group. Group statement (covers a whole group of plants, not this species by name). Shown as context, not counted.", "note": "Covers willows as a group. Group statement (covers a whole group of plants, not this species by name). Shown as context, not counted.", "short": "Gerard (1633)", "source": "John Gerard, The Herball or Generall Historie of Plantes, enlarged by Thomas Johnson (1633 text; read in the Ex-Classics transcription and checked against the 1636 printing scanned at archive.org)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Galenic (European)", "url": "https://www.exclassics.com/herbal/herball.txt", "year": "1633"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. Leaves, not bark. Shown, not counted.", "assigns_moisture": "Dry", "assigns_temperature": "Cool", "corpus": "galenic-european", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "Salix. Willow leaves, are cold, dry, and binding", "gloss": "Willow leaves are cold and dry.", "locator": "Catalogue of simples, Herbs (Gutenberg #49513 line ~17232)", "not_counted_why": "Leaves, not bark. Shown, not counted.", "note": "Leaves, not bark. Shown, not counted.", "short": "Culpeper (1653)", "source": "Nicholas Culpeper, The Complete Herbal (text of 1653; London: Thomas Kelly, 1850 edition as digitised by Project Gutenberg #49513)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Galenic (European)", "url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/49513/pg49513.txt", "year": "1653"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. Species problem: Chinese 柳 is the weeping willow (Salix babylonica), not S. alba. Not counted.", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cold", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "柳華 … 氣味苦寒無毒 … 枝及根白皮氣味 {同華}", "gloss": "Willow flower bitter, cold; branch and root bark the same.", "locator": "卷三十五下 木之二, 柳", "not_counted_why": "Species problem: Chinese 柳 is the weeping willow (Salix babylonica), not S. alba. Not counted.", "note": "Species problem: Chinese 柳 is the weeping willow (Salix babylonica), not S. alba. Not counted.", "short": "Bencao Gangmu (1596)", "source": "李時珍, 本草綱目 (Li Shizhen, Bencao Gangmu), Siku Quanshu text", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草綱目_(四庫全書本)/", "year": "1596"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. Flower, and S. babylonica. Not counted.", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cold", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "柳花　味苦，寒。", "gloss": "Willow flower (catkin): bitter, cold.", "locator": "下經, 柳花", "not_counted_why": "Flower, and S. babylonica. Not counted.", "note": "Flower, and S. babylonica. Not counted.", "short": "Shennong Bencao Jing (c. 200 CE)", "source": "神農本草經 (Shennong Bencao Jing, c. 200 CE), Sun Xingyan recension", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/神農本草經_(孫星衍)", "year": "c. 200 CE (recension 1799)"}], "sources_agree": false, "stored_before": {"moisture": "Dry", "temperature": "Cold"}, "stored_value_status": {"moisture": {"status": "clear", "why": "a definite Dry"}, "temperature": {"status": "clear", "why": "a definite Cold"}}}$j$::jsonb);

-- H170 Goji / Wolfberry (Gou Qi Zi) (batch 1, 5 sources, SOURCES DISAGREE)
insert into _energetics_batch values ('H170', $j${"agreement_state": "disagree", "app_value": {"moisture": "Moist", "temperature": "Neutral"}, "app_value_changed": {"moisture": false, "temperature": false}, "app_value_lines": {"moisture": "stays Moist (clear modern value; old sources agree)", "temperature": "stays Neutral (clear modern value; old sources disagree, shown on page)"}, "batch": 1, "checked_no_reading": ["Porter Smith 1871: files the fruit under 'Berberis Lycium' ('tonic, cooling, demulcent'), a misidentification and an action list; not qualifying"], "counted_readings": {"moisture": [{"reading": "Moist", "source": "Bencao Gangmu (1596)"}, {"reading": "Moist", "source": "Bencao Congxin (1757)"}], "temperature": [{"reading": "Neutral", "source": "Bencao Gangmu (1596)"}, {"reading": "Warm", "source": "Bencao Congxin (1757)"}]}, "disagreement_text": "On temperature, the old sources disagree: Bencao Gangmu (1596) reads it as neutral; Bencao Congxin (1757) reads it as warm. The app keeps neutral, the modern reading of what the herb does in the body; the old readings are shown here but do not change it.", "no_pre1900_source_found": false, "notes": ["BCGM names Gansu (甘州) fruit as the best, the home of Lycium barbarum; the older Chinese texts do not separate L. chinense from L. barbarum."], "part_used": "Ripe fruit (berry), dried", "researched": "2026-09-15", "rule": "Temperature: stored value clear (a definite Neutral per Chinese materia medica), so it stays Neutral. Moisture: stored value clear (a definite Moist), so it stays Moist.", "rule_general": "FINAL founder rules 2026-09-15: clear stored modern value stays; unclear or missing value set by majority of first-hand pre-1900 sources; tie broken by the oldest first-hand written source, Neutral if the oldest sources are themselves tied; copied readings count once; group statements, second-hand reports, other parts and other species shown but not counted; snigdha and 潤 = Moist, rūkṣa and 燥 = Dry.", "sources": [{"agreement": "Counted: agrees with the app temperature (neutral); agrees with the app moisture (moist).", "assigns_moisture": "Moist", "assigns_temperature": "Neutral", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": true, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "竊謂枸杞苖葉味苦甘而氣凉根味甘淡氣寒子味甘氣平 … 至于子則甘平而潤性滋而補", "gloss": "Li Shizhen's own judgement: shoots and leaves bitter-sweet and cool, root bland and cold, the FRUIT sweet and NEUTRAL; and in his discussion, the fruit is sweet, neutral and MOISTENING, its nature nourishing.", "locator": "卷三十六 木之三, 枸杞地骨皮, 氣味 note and 發明 (時珍曰)", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "Li argues the Shennong 'bitter, cold' reading covered the whole plant. 潤 counts as Moist under the final rules.", "short": "Bencao Gangmu (1596)", "source": "李時珍, 本草綱目 (Li Shizhen, Bencao Gangmu), Siku Quanshu text", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草綱目_(四庫全書本)/", "year": "1596"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. The heading repeats the whole-plant Shennong value; Li Shizhen's own note is used instead (founder rule). Shown, not counted.", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cold", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "枸杞子 … 氣味苦寒 {權曰甘平}", "gloss": "Fruit section heading: bitter, cold (Zhen Quan: sweet, neutral).", "locator": "卷三十六, 枸杞子 subsection heading", "not_counted_why": "The heading repeats the whole-plant Shennong value; Li Shizhen's own note is used instead (founder rule). Shown, not counted.", "note": "The heading repeats the whole-plant Shennong value; Li Shizhen's own note is used instead (founder rule). Shown, not counted.", "short": "Bencao Gangmu (1596)", "source": "李時珍, 本草綱目 (Li Shizhen, Bencao Gangmu), Siku Quanshu text", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草綱目_(四庫全書本)/", "year": "1596"}, {"agreement": "Counted: differs from the app temperature (source warm, app neutral); agrees with the app moisture (moist).", "assigns_moisture": "Moist", "assigns_temperature": "Warm", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": true, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "枸杞子 滋補肝腎、而潤。甘微溫。滋肝益腎。… 然味甘性潤，仍是補水之藥", "gloss": "Goji fruit: nourishes liver and kidney, and MOISTENS; sweet, slightly warm. Its taste is sweet and its nature MOISTENING.", "locator": "卷九 木部, 枸杞子", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "Not a word-for-word copy of Li Shizhen (Congxin reads slightly warm, not neutral), so it counts separately.", "short": "Bencao Congxin (1757)", "source": "吳儀洛, 本草從新 (Wu Yiluo, Bencao Congxin)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草從新", "year": "1757"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. Whole plant, not the fruit specifically.", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cold", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "味苦，寒。主五內邪氣，熱中消渴，周痹。", "gloss": "Lycium (whole plant): bitter, cold.", "locator": "上經, 枸杞", "not_counted_why": "Whole plant, not the fruit specifically.", "note": "Whole plant, not the fruit specifically.", "short": "Shennong Bencao Jing (c. 200 CE)", "source": "神農本草經 (Shennong Bencao Jing, c. 200 CE), Sun Xingyan recension", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/神農本草經_(孫星衍)", "year": "c. 200 CE (recension 1799)"}, {"agreement": "Shown for context. A second-hand report: the text credits another writer.", "assigns_moisture": null, "assigns_temperature": "Cool", "corpus": "chinese", "counted": false, "counted_moisture": false, "counted_temperature": false, "excerpt": "别錄曰根大寒子微寒", "gloss": "Bielu: root very cold, fruit slightly cold.", "locator": "卷三十六, 枸杞 氣味 note", "not_counted_why": "A second-hand report: the text credits another writer.", "note": "", "short": "Bencao Gangmu (1596)", "source": "李時珍, 本草綱目 (Li Shizhen, Bencao Gangmu), Siku Quanshu text", "tier": "second-hand-report", "tradition": "Chinese", "url": "https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/本草綱目_(四庫全書本)/", "year": "1596"}], "sources_agree": false, "stored_before": {"moisture": "Moist", "temperature": "Neutral"}, "stored_value_status": {"moisture": {"status": "clear", "why": "a definite Moist"}, "temperature": {"status": "clear", "why": "a definite Neutral per Chinese materia medica"}}}$j$::jsonb);

